1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Millions of Indian shops run on a paper khata. Khata keeps the habit and does the bookkeeping.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:24,000
"Ramesh ko paanch sau udhaar" means "500 on credit to Ramesh". Just speak.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Pick what it is: Bill, Entry or Udhaar. Confirm, and it shows what Ramesh owes now.

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Make a bill in chat. It remembers rates and lets you change them.

5
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Done: a PDF bill, added to Ramesh's account.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Photograph a handwritten bill. It reads every line.

7
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:25,000
It caught the mistake: 3 × ₹45 is ₹135, not ₹145. Nothing is saved yet.

8
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The shopkeeper may only ever open the Google Sheet, so it works both ways.

9
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Change an amount in the sheet, and the bot knows.

10
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Any table, as PDF or Excel.

11
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Customers who owe money become ghosts. The séance drafts a polite reminder. You choose whether to send it.

12
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Stitched from Telegram, Whisper, vision, Sheets and SQLite on free tiers. Built with Kiro specs, steering, hooks, a custom agent and property-based tests.
